            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0279" n="214" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg214"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.00111 Armament Control/984: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-04T10:00:00+01:00">August 4, 1936—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 4—9:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>310. Department’s 71, June 20, 1 p.m. Embassy would appreciate any expression of
                    opinion the Department would care to give as to the nature of the reply which
                    should be made to requests now being received from American firms for assistance
                    in connection with trade transactions with Italy entered into subsequent to the
                    Department’s telegram No. 200, November 13, 6 p.m., 1935,<anchor n="68"
                        xml:id="d213-f1"/> regarding trade promotion activities in Italy and prior
                    to the Department’s telegram 71 of June 20th revoking the instruction contained
                    therein.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
